rowing borrowing need: the liability benchmark shows the net loans requirement rising from \u00a3142.0m to \u00a3191.1m by March 2028 while existing loans amortise down to \u00a3136.8m \u2014 roughly \u00a364m of new borrowing to find within two years if the capital programme is delivered as planned. Only 7% of debt matures within 12 months, well inside the 25% limit.","fy":"2025/26","as_of_doc":"Treasury Management Outturn report 2025/26 (AG192)","as_of_url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk/documents/s35422/AG192 Treasury management outturn 25-26.pdf","as_of_date":"2026-07-16","signals":[{"code":"borrowing-increase","headline":"Net loans requirement rises from \u00a3142.0m at 31/3/26 to \u00a3191.1m by 31/3/28; liability benchmark of \u00a3201.1m vs existing borrowing falling to \u00a3136.8m implies ~\u00a364m of new external borrowing within two years","why":"A dated, quantified pipeline of new PWLB/market borrowing demand driven by the housing capital programme."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"cfr","value":"\u00a3280.8m total (General Fund \u00a368.3m, HRA \u00a3212.5m); Loans CFR \u00a3278.1m","as_at":"31/03/26","page":6},{"name":"borrowing","value":"\u00a3159.3m, all PWLB and all HRA-related, weighted average rate 3.06%, weighted average maturity 17.8 years","as_at":"31/03/26","page":8},{"name":"new borrowing in year","value":"\u00a310m new PWLB (two \u00a35m EIP tranches, December and March) less \u00a35m maturity and \u00a30.2m EIP repayments","as_at":"2025/26","page":8},{"name":"investments","value":"\u00a316.6m total (\u00a311.6m short-term/cash at 3.73%, \u00a35m pooled property fund at 4.67% income return); balances ranged \u00a316.6m-\u00a351.0m in year","as_at":"31/03/26","page":9},{"name":"internal borrowing","value":"\u00a3118.8m (decreased \u00a36.3m in year)","as_at":"31/03/26","page":6},{"name":"maturity under 12m","value":"7% of fixed-rate borrowing (upper limit 25%)","as_at":"31/03/26","page":15},{"name":"treasury outturn vs budget","value":"inves