tee":"Cabinet","time":"9.30 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-03","committee":"Cabinet Committee: Housing","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-04","committee":"Council","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-12","committee":"The Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-08-20","committee":"Council","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-08-25","committee":"Cabinet","time":"9.30 am","status":"Confirmed; Additional meeting","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-07","committee":"The Scrutiny Committee","time":"6.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","time":"9.30 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet Member for Good Homes Decision Day","time":"1.00 pm","status":"Provisional","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Significant deferrals across Subject to Appraisal projects, with \u00a36.25m of \u00a38.4m budget removed from 2026/27 forecast","lead":"Substantial deferrals in capital programme create uncertainty about timing of capital expenditure and may indicate spending constraints or delayed project readiness","iso":"2026-09-09","paper_title":"CAB3567 Appendix 5","paper_url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk/documents/s35881/35881.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"River Park leisure centre demolition deferred from 2026/27 and budget reduced following costings","lead":"Material capital project deferrals and budget reductions indicate either cost pressures or execution delays on major projects, affecting cash flow and borrowing needs","iso":"2026-09-09","paper_title":"CAB3567 Appendix 5","paper_url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk/documents/s35881/35881.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Sewage treatment works budget of \u00a30.4m insufficient for four planned upgrades; only three will proceed","lead":"Insufficient budget to complete planned maintenance works suggests either cost underestimation or delayed delivery of planned efficiency improvements that would reduce ongoing HRA operating subsidy requirements.","iso":"2026-09-09","paper_title":"CAB3568 Housing Revenue Account (HRA) Outturn 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk/documents/s35879/35879.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"CAB3567 Appendix 5","paper_url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk/documents/s35881/35881.pdf","headline":"Significant deferrals across Subject to Appraisal projects, with \u00a36.25m of \u00a38.4m budget removed from 2026/27 forecast","detail":"The Subject to Appraisal section originally budgeted \u00a38.4m but only \u00a31.6m is now forecast for 2026/27, representing \u00a36.25m of deferrals. Major deferrals include: leisure centre demolition (\u00a32m), LEP applications (\u00a32m), CWR CIL infrastructure (\u00a31m), and Brooks car park air handling unit works (\u00a31m). Projects are being pushed into 2027/28 or pending approval.","category":"capital","matters":"Substantial deferrals in capital programme create uncertainty about timing of capital expenditure and may indicate spending constraints or delayed project readiness","figures":"Subject to Appraisal original budget \u00a38,415k, other changes -\u00a36,250k, forecast \u00a31,580k","quote":"Now expected in 2027/28","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"CAB3567 Appendix 5","paper_url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk/documents/s35881/35881.pdf","headline":"River Park leisure centre demolition deferred from 2026/27 and budget reduced following costings","detail":"The leisure centre demolition was a \u00a32m Subject to Appraisal project for 2026/27 that has now been completely removed from this year's forecast and reprofiled to 2027/28. The council notes that the budget has been reduced following costings, indicating either cost pressures or scope adjustments have emerged.","category":"capital","matters":"Material capital project deferrals and budget reductions indicate either cost pressures or execution delays on major projects, affecting cash flow and borrowing needs","figures":"\u00a32,000k originally budgeted, now \u00a30 forecast for 2026/27","quote":"Reprofiled to 27/28 and budget reduced following costings","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"CAB3568 Housing Revenue Account (HRA) Outturn 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk/documents/s35879/35879.pdf","headline":"Sewage treatment works budget of \u00a30.4m insufficient for four planned upgrades; only three will proceed","detail":"The Cabinet had set aside \u00a30.4m for sewage site upgrade works to reduce running costs and reduce HRA subsidy to treatment sites. Following initial feasibility work, the council now estimates this budget will only fund three plant upgrades rather than the originally intended four. Additional budget requests will be made as business cases are developed for the fourth site.","category":"capital","matters":"Insufficient budget to complete planned maintenance works suggests either cost underestimation or delayed delivery of planned efficiency improvements that would reduce ongoing HRA operating subsidy requirements.","figures":"\u00a30.4m budget, originally intended for four site upgrades, now sufficient for three upgrades only","quote":"Note that the \u00a30.4m for sewerage site upgrade works set by Cabinet at its meeting of September 2024 is now only sufficient to fund three plant upgrades, rather than the originally intended four, and that additional budget requests will be made as business cases are developed.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"CAB3568 Housing Revenue Account (HRA) Outturn 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk/documents/s35879/35879.pdf","headline":"Right to Buy sales spiked to 33 properties in 2025/26, significantly above historic average but expected to decline","detail":"The council sold 33 properties under Right to Buy in 2025/26, significantly higher than historic average and higher than the increased budget assumption. The council notes that changes to the RTB scheme implemented in late 2024/25 \"make the scheme significantly less attractive\" and sales are expected to reduce in future years. The spike and subsequent decline will affect both housing stock numbers and rental income.","category":"income","matters":"Material RTB sales volatility affects the council's housing stock base, rental income trajectory, and the availability of RTB 1-4-1 receipts for reinvestment in new affordable housing, which is a key council priority.","figures":"33 RTB sales in 2025/26, adverse income variance \u00a30.398m partially attributable to RTB sales and void properties","quote":"Thirty three properties were sold under right to buy in 2025/26, which is significantly higher than historic average.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"CAB3568 Housing Revenue Account (HRA) Outturn 2025-26","paper_url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk/documents/s35879/35879.pdf","headline":"Climate change retrofit programme \u00a33.262m underspend; delivery strategy underwent redesign following delays","detail":"The climate change emergency budget of \u00a35.336m in 2025/26 spent only \u00a32.074m, a \u00a33.26m underspend (61%). Delays in fabric works were caused by SHF Wave 3 documentation requirements and DESNZ holding battery installations. The SHF funding was rescinded, impacting construction schedules. The team redesigned the retrofit delivery strategy and piloted two new contractors. Underspent budget is being reprofiled to 2026-27 and beyond.","category":"capital","matters":"The programme restructuring and substantial slippage (61% underspend) raise delivery risk on the council's commitment to achieve EPC-C ratings on all stock by 2030, a key climate/energy performance objective.","figures":"Revised budget \u00a35.336m, outturn \u00a32.074m, variance \u00a33.262m, \u00a30.345m carried forward to 2026/27 for Swedish Cottages insulation pilots","quote":"The SHF funding was rescinded, which took time and impacted on the construction contract programme of works.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-09"},"name":"Winchester","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-17","since_iso":"2026-08-18","distress":false,"headline":"Significant deferrals across Subject to Appraisal projects, with \u00a36.25m of \u00a38.4m budget removed from 2026/27 forecast","lead":"Substantial deferrals in capital programme create uncertainty about timing of capital expenditure and may indicate spending constraints or delayed project readiness","also":["24 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit and Governance Committee on 2026-09-24","n_findings":25,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"CAB3567 Appendix 5","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.winchester.gov.uk/documents/s35881/35881.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":71,"news_drafts_total":3}}